cases.Description:
Operations is asking if we can create a rule to hold orders and prevent them from picking until an operator reviews them and cancels or approves them for picking. 

The logic would be to identify the WMS order number either through the payload in the integration or in the application or DB layer when the order is created to check if that wms order number exists currently in a status other than complete, canceled or abandoned. If it identifies an order, both orders are put on hold and need reviewed. 

What is happening is operations is waving the same order multiple times causing duplicate picks to GM. 

To identify the wms order number, it is provided within the GM order or WMS wave number as the %SO# part. It's also found within the payload as order.number.  For example below WMS order would be SO9910545.
